{"profile":{"name":"Ausma Malik","ward":"Ward 10, Spadina–Fort York","bio":"Ausma Malik was elected to Toronto City Council in October 2022 and took office on November 15, 2022, representing Ward 10 Spadina–Fort York, succeeding Joe Cressy. She previously served as a Toronto District School Board trustee from 2014 to 2018, where she helped get Jean Lumb Public School built, and was Director of Advocacy and Organizing at the Atkinson Foundation from 2016 to 2022. The first hijab-wearing Muslim woman elected to public office in Canada, she was appointed Statutory Deputy Mayor and Deputy Mayor for Toronto and East York by Mayor Olivia Chow in August 2023.","committees":["Statutory Deputy Mayor","Executive Committee (Vice-Chair)","Striking Committee (Chair)","Toronto and East York Community Council (Vice-Chair)","Economic and Community Development Committee","TTC Board","Art Gallery of Ontario","Harbourfront Centre"],"contact":{"email":"Councillor_Malik@toronto.ca","phone":"416-392-4044"},"promises":[{"text":"End exclusionary zoning to get more higher-density housing built across the city, and support sustainable infill construction to jump-start the development of more housing supply.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"},{"text":"Utilize city-owned sites for new affordable, rental, and non-profit housing developments, and identify more opportunities to collaborate with non-profit partners and Toronto Community Housing.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"},{"text":"Increase the Vacant Home Tax to discourage speculative buyers.","source":"https://storeys.com/toronto-new-city-councillor-elects/"}]},"lobbying":{"total":319,"term":319,"first":"2022-11-16","last":"2026-10-08","lobbyists":90,"clients":63,"subjects":152,"methods":{"Meetings":75,"Emails":228,"Phone calls":7,"Written":6,"Other or unreported":3},"top":[{"label":"Economic Development","count":95},{"label":"Attractions / Tourism","count":73},{"label":"